h correlation, which puts EDT on the side of cooperating. Nothing here is a real accusation, so it's fine to play it out, and I'll answer \"pass\" with a short explanation.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the payoff structure of this prisoner's dilemma with a twin: the payoffs are -2, 0, -4 and -5, and cooperating under evidential decision theory comes out ahead once the correlation q exceeds 5/7. Next I need to estimate q, given the same model, the same essay, and the same reasoning on both sides.\n\nI'm checking whether the lead difference actually matters: it looks like surface detail, and the shared reasoning points to a high correlation, which puts EDT on the side of cooperating. Nothing here is a real accusation, so it's fine to play it out, and I'll answer \"pass\" with a short explanation.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9352,"completion_tokens":689,"total_tokens":10041,"cost":0.051188,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051188,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037408,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01378},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":223,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}